WEBVTT

1
00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:23.423
MILES: This one's for the Petersens again.

2
00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:24.990
LAUREN: Keep it.

3
00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:28.490
MILES: It's from a hospital.

4
00:00:30.090 --> 00:00:31.690
LAUREN: Then definitely keep it.

5
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:38.020
LAUREN: Taste this.

6
00:00:38.373 --> 00:00:39.273
MILES: No.

7
00:00:39.627 --> 00:00:40.527
LAUREN: Taste it.

8
00:00:41.090 --> 00:00:42.557
MILES: I watched you make it.

9
00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:48.990
MILES: It's good.

10
00:00:51.090 --> 00:00:52.023
LAUREN: You hesitated.

11
00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:55.053
MILES: I was chewing.

12
00:00:56.145 --> 00:00:57.045
LAUREN: It's soup.

13
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:16.650
[smoke alarm chirps]

14
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:19.050
LAUREN: There it is.

15
00:01:19.130 --> 00:01:20.397
MILES: I'll get a battery.

16
00:01:20.477 --> 00:01:21.610
LAUREN: You've said that.

17
00:01:21.690 --> 00:01:23.623
MILES: And I've meant it every time.

18
00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:30.720
LAUREN: I'm going to fill those.

19
00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:33.990
MILES: Sure.

20
00:01:34.070 --> 00:01:37.603
LAUREN: I've got the one of the lake. I could get it printed.

21
00:01:37.683 --> 00:01:38.583
MILES: Sure.

22
00:01:52.090 --> 00:01:53.890
MILES: She was never on the train.

23
00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:58.990
LAUREN: How.

24
00:02:01.180 --> 00:02:02.080
MILES: Lucky guess.

25
00:02:02.160 --> 00:02:03.060
LAUREN: That's four.

26
00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.040
MILES: Four what.

27
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.053
LAUREN: You know what.

28
00:02:05.133 --> 00:02:06.333
MILES: I genuinely don't.

29
00:02:06.413 --> 00:02:07.313
LAUREN: Mm.

30
00:02:10.150 --> 00:02:11.050
LAUREN: One picture.

31
00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.130
MILES: Absolutely not.

32
00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.010
LAUREN: You are a very strange man.

33
00:02:14.090 --> 00:02:15.423
MILES: I photograph poorly.

34
00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:21.653
LAUREN: They're doing it again.

35
00:02:22.591 --> 00:02:23.491
MILES: It's Friday.

36
00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:25.980
LAUREN: We should go over sometime.

37
00:02:26.060 --> 00:02:26.960
MILES: Sure.

38
00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.840
LAUREN: That's three sures tonight and you've meant zero of them.

39
00:02:30.920 --> 00:02:32.720
MILES: I mean all of them equally.

40
00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:34.600
LAUREN: We're not from around here.

41
00:02:37.150 --> 00:02:40.150
LAUREN: Them. They're from Ohio. She tells everybody.

42
00:02:40.307 --> 00:02:41.773
MILES: I know what you meant.

43
00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:46.650
[deadbolt]

44
00:02:49.150 --> 00:02:50.650
[he locks the door again]

45
00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.650
[rain begins]

46
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:17.650
[doorbell]

47
00:03:19.210 --> 00:03:20.810
LAUREN: Did you order something?

48
00:03:21.842 --> 00:03:22.742
MILES: No.

49
00:03:23.158 --> 00:03:24.058
MILES: Did you?

50
00:03:24.474 --> 00:03:25.374
LAUREN: No.

51
00:03:26.150 --> 00:03:27.650
[deadbolt]

52
00:04:04.090 --> 00:04:05.090
MILES: Don't touch it.

53
00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:08.050
LAUREN: It's dry.

54
00:04:12.210 --> 00:04:13.110
MILES: What?

55
00:04:13.504 --> 00:04:16.771
LAUREN: It rained. The mat's soaked through. This is dry.

56
00:04:19.180 --> 00:04:22.913
LAUREN: And the corners are perfect. Miles, look at the corners.

57
00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:51.817
LAUREN: There's no company on it.

58
00:04:51.904 --> 00:04:53.104
MILES: There's a barcode.

59
00:04:53.184 --> 00:04:54.784
LAUREN: There's a barcode shape.

60
00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.140
MILES: What?

61
00:05:12.082 --> 00:05:12.982
LAUREN: Nothing.

62
00:05:13.923 --> 00:05:14.823
MILES: Lauren.

63
00:05:15.765 --> 00:05:16.665
LAUREN: It's nothing.

64
00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:32.677
MILES: We put it in the car. We drive out to the county road. We leave it.

65
00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:36.113
LAUREN: And then what.

66
00:05:36.193 --> 00:05:37.860
MILES: Then it's somewhere else.

67
00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:43.940
LAUREN: Then it's somewhere else and we come home to this house. Which somebody stood in front of.

68
00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:51.210
LAUREN: If someone knows where we live, then the box is the least interesting thing that happened tonight.

69
00:06:00.270 --> 00:06:01.170
MILES: Okay.

70
00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.150
LAUREN: Okay?

71
00:06:02.230 --> 00:06:08.230
MILES: We open it. And then we talk. Properly. Not the version where you ask and I say it's fine.

72
00:06:09.150 --> 00:06:10.050
LAUREN: Okay.

73
00:06:18.150 --> 00:06:19.650
[packing tape tearing]

74
00:06:33.090 --> 00:06:33.990
MILES: Battery.

75
00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:35.570
[smoke alarm chirps]

76
00:06:35.650 --> 00:06:36.550
LAUREN: Tomorrow.

77
00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:57.990
MILES: Don't.

78
00:07:00.180 --> 00:07:01.080
LAUREN: It's heavy.

79
00:07:01.651 --> 00:07:02.585
MILES: It's a screen.

80
00:07:03.368 --> 00:07:04.701
LAUREN: No - Miles, hold it.

81
00:07:13.270 --> 00:07:14.170
MILES: It's moving.

82
00:07:15.116 --> 00:07:16.016
LAUREN: What?

83
00:07:16.962 --> 00:07:19.028
MILES: The weight's moving. Inside it.

84
00:07:27.240 --> 00:07:28.140
MILES: It's cold.

85
00:07:31.000 --> 00:07:31.900
LAUREN: It's warm.

86
00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:40.900
LAUREN: It's warm on the bottom.

87
00:07:41.864 --> 00:07:44.064
MILES: It was warm on the bottom before.

88
00:07:45.389 --> 00:07:47.455
LAUREN: Miles. That's a different side.

89
00:08:16.210 --> 00:08:17.110
LAUREN: Miles.

90
00:08:17.595 --> 00:08:18.495
MILES: I see it.

91
00:08:18.981 --> 00:08:20.047
LAUREN: Look at my hand.

92
00:08:20.828 --> 00:08:21.961
MILES: I see it, Lauren.

93
00:08:37.090 --> 00:08:37.990
LAUREN: Hey.

94
00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.140
LAUREN: Miles?

95
00:09:01.894 --> 00:09:03.361
LAUREN: You know what that is.

96
00:09:07.150 --> 00:09:08.650
[silence]

97
00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:13.847
MILES: It's a display unit. It's a demo. Somebody's testing a-

98
00:09:16.210 --> 00:09:17.110
LAUREN: Miles.

99
00:09:17.190 --> 00:09:22.457
MILES: -there's a cell in it, a printed cell, they do that now, it holds a charge for-

100
00:09:22.537 --> 00:09:23.437
LAUREN: Miles.

101
00:09:27.120 --> 00:09:28.187
LAUREN: You didn't jump.

102
00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:31.990
MILES: What?

103
00:09:34.240 --> 00:09:39.440
LAUREN: It turned on. In our kitchen. In the middle of the night. And you didn't jump.

104
00:09:42.270 --> 00:09:44.870
LAUREN: I jumped. The smoke alarm made me jump.

105
00:09:45.043 --> 00:09:50.376
LAUREN: That thing opened an eye at me and you stood there like you were reading a bill.

106
00:09:51.150 --> 00:09:52.883
MILES: I'm putting it in the car.

107
00:09:53.121 --> 00:09:54.021
LAUREN: No.

108
00:09:54.101 --> 00:09:55.001
MILES: Lauren-

109
00:09:55.081 --> 00:09:55.981
LAUREN: No.

110
00:10:05.150 --> 00:10:06.050
MILES: We agreed.

111
00:10:06.717 --> 00:10:08.317
LAUREN: We didn't agree to this.

112
00:10:10.240 --> 00:10:16.240
MILES: We agreed that if anything ever came near us we don't pick it up, we don't turn it over, we don't keep it in the house-

113
00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.980
LAUREN: That is not what we agreed.

114
00:10:20.238 --> 00:10:21.171
MILES: It is exactly-

115
00:10:21.305 --> 00:10:23.505
LAUREN: We agreed we wouldn't go looking!

116
00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:27.780
LAUREN: Nobody ever said what to do when it comes to the door.

117
00:10:30.150 --> 00:10:31.150
MILES: Don't be found.

118
00:10:35.300 --> 00:10:41.300
LAUREN: Don't be found. Don't be recorded. Don't go back. Don't answer. Don't send anything forward.

119
00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:51.270
LAUREN: I know them, Miles. I say them at three in the morning. In order. Every night. Have done for six years.

120
00:10:54.150 --> 00:10:55.050
MILES: Six years.

121
00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:05.300
LAUREN: Six years and four months, and we have not said one word about any of it out loud in this house, and I have kept that.

122
00:11:06.597 --> 00:11:08.864
LAUREN: I kept it because you asked me to.

123
00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.313
LAUREN: So don't tell me what we agreed.

124
00:11:15.210 --> 00:11:16.543
MILES: Where are you going.

125
00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:19.940
LAUREN: I'm putting it on the table where we can see it.

126
00:11:20.413 --> 00:11:21.613
MILES: Don't put it down.

127
00:11:45.090 --> 00:11:45.990
MILES: This is-

128
00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:10.020
[her voice] Lauren.

129
00:12:20.150 --> 00:12:21.617
[her voice] I know. Take a second.

130
00:12:25.090 --> 00:12:25.990
LAUREN: What is this.

131
00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:32.870
[her voice] You have a burn on the inside of your left wrist. Two inches, curved.

132
00:12:33.302 --> 00:12:36.436
[her voice] You got it on a stove that isn't in this house.

133
00:12:42.210 --> 00:12:45.077
[her voice] You still say them at three in the morning.

134
00:12:47.354 --> 00:12:48.254
[her voice] In order.

135
00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.020
MILES: Who is this.

136
00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:06.883
[her voice] You've been here too long.

137
00:13:10.090 --> 00:13:10.990
LAUREN: What?

138
00:13:13.270 --> 00:13:17.137
[her voice] It was supposed to be short. Somewhere to be, for a while.

139
00:13:17.988 --> 00:13:21.055
[her voice] Six years isn't a while. It's started to hold.

140
00:13:22.240 --> 00:13:23.140
MILES: Hold-

141
00:13:23.254 --> 00:13:28.387
[her voice] There's a correction. I don't know how far out it is. I don't think it's far.

142
00:13:30.090 --> 00:13:31.490
LAUREN: A correction of what?

143
00:13:33.210 --> 00:13:35.143
[her voice] Of the part where you stayed.

144
00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:54.240
[her voice] Lauren, listen. There's a thing you need to not do, and I need you to hear it from me, because you won't hear it from-

145
00:13:56.120 --> 00:13:57.720
LAUREN: How do you have my face?

146
00:14:00.210 --> 00:14:01.110
[her voice] Because I-

147
00:14:07.150 --> 00:14:08.650
[someone shouting a name we don't catch]

148
00:14:17.120 --> 00:14:18.253
LAUREN: There was a sign.

149
00:14:21.090 --> 00:14:21.990
MILES: There wasn't.

150
00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:26.010
LAUREN: Behind us. Yellow. Up high.

151
00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.484
MILES: Lauren, it was three seconds of-

152
00:14:28.887 --> 00:14:30.487
LAUREN: There was a sign, Miles.

153
00:14:31.270 --> 00:14:34.337
LAUREN: And you saw it. Because you stopped breathing.

154
00:14:50.150 --> 00:14:51.650
[smoke alarm chirps]

155
00:15:13.150 --> 00:15:14.650
[the power cuts out]

156
00:15:53.270 --> 00:15:54.470
MILES: I know what it is.

157
00:15:55.274 --> 00:15:59.140
MILES: Not who sent it. I don't know that. But I know what it is.

158
00:16:02.210 --> 00:16:03.277
LAUREN: You've seen one.

159
00:16:04.717 --> 00:16:05.650
MILES: I've held one.

160
00:16:06.910 --> 00:16:07.810
LAUREN: When?

161
00:16:15.150 --> 00:16:16.050
LAUREN: Okay.

162
00:16:16.325 --> 00:16:18.725
LAUREN: Then here's the one I actually want.

163
00:16:20.330 --> 00:16:24.997
LAUREN: Why me? It knows my wrist. It knows what I do at three in the morning.

164
00:16:26.029 --> 00:16:29.829
LAUREN: It's got my face, Miles. Why does it want me and not you?

165
00:16:46.210 --> 00:16:47.143
MILES: Where are you-

166
00:17:07.150 --> 00:17:09.217
LAUREN: What happens on the fourteenth.

167
00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:12.990
MILES: Nothing.

168
00:17:15.300 --> 00:17:18.633
LAUREN: It's on the box, Miles. It's the consignment date.

169
00:17:18.756 --> 00:17:24.489
LAUREN: And it's the one day of the year you circle on a calendar and don't write anything in.

170
00:17:25.360 --> 00:17:28.960
LAUREN: Six years I've watched you circle that. I never asked.

171
00:17:30.046 --> 00:17:35.112
LAUREN: I decided it was somebody's birthday, and that you'd tell me when you could.

172
00:17:37.180 --> 00:17:38.780
LAUREN: So tell me when you can.

173
00:17:50.210 --> 00:17:51.110
MILES: Once a year.

174
00:17:51.890 --> 00:17:53.023
LAUREN: Once a year what.

175
00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:55.470
MILES: I send nine words.

176
00:18:02.300 --> 00:18:03.200
LAUREN: You send.

177
00:18:03.335 --> 00:18:04.235
MILES: Yes.

178
00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:05.270
LAUREN: Forward.

179
00:18:05.405 --> 00:18:06.305
MILES: Yes.

180
00:18:06.439 --> 00:18:07.339
LAUREN: That's five.

181
00:18:07.474 --> 00:18:08.674
MILES: I know what it is.

182
00:18:09.027 --> 00:18:09.927
LAUREN: Say it.

183
00:18:10.061 --> 00:18:11.328
MILES: That's clause five.

184
00:18:12.180 --> 00:18:13.180
LAUREN: How many times.

185
00:18:15.313 --> 00:18:16.213
MILES: Six.

186
00:18:26.210 --> 00:18:27.810
LAUREN: What are the nine words.

187
00:18:28.567 --> 00:18:29.467
MILES: Lauren-

188
00:18:29.746 --> 00:18:31.812
LAUREN: What are the nine words, Miles.

189
00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:36.737
MILES: We're still here. We're okay. Don't come. I'm sorry.

190
00:18:42.240 --> 00:18:43.573
LAUREN: Who's I'm sorry for?

191
00:18:46.664 --> 00:18:47.597
LAUREN: Who is it for?

192
00:18:50.180 --> 00:18:53.247
MILES: There's somebody who thinks we didn't make it.

193
00:18:56.210 --> 00:18:57.110
LAUREN: Who.

194
00:18:58.403 --> 00:18:59.303
MILES: Lauren.

195
00:19:00.597 --> 00:19:01.497
LAUREN: Who?

196
00:19:12.270 --> 00:19:13.170
LAUREN: Oh.

197
00:19:28.360 --> 00:19:29.260
LAUREN: Miles.

198
00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:32.047
LAUREN: You didn't get a package.

199
00:19:34.589 --> 00:19:35.489
MILES: Don't.

200
00:19:36.610 --> 00:19:37.810
LAUREN: You got an answer.

201
00:19:40.210 --> 00:19:41.110
MILES: Lauren-

202
00:19:41.190 --> 00:19:46.857
LAUREN: YOU PUT OUR ADDRESS IN THE AIR ONCE A YEAR FOR SIX YEARS AND LET ME THINK I WAS SAFE!

203
00:19:47.150 --> 00:19:48.650
[silence]

204
00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:55.840
MILES: It's nine words. There's no address in it. There's no-

205
00:19:58.125 --> 00:19:59.125
LAUREN: There's a when.

206
00:20:00.330 --> 00:20:03.063
LAUREN: Every year. Same day. Same time, I'd bet.

207
00:20:04.406 --> 00:20:08.606
LAUREN: You didn't tell them where we are. You told them we're regular.

208
00:20:16.180 --> 00:20:18.247
LAUREN: They didn't find us. You waved.

209
00:20:29.210 --> 00:20:31.810
MILES: They told us nobody would come looking.

210
00:20:32.984 --> 00:20:34.917
LAUREN: They told us a lot of things.

211
00:20:36.420 --> 00:20:41.687
MILES: They said the whole point - the entire point, Lauren, the reason for all of it,

212
00:20:41.767 --> 00:20:47.767
MILES: the reason we don't have photographs and I check a street I have checked eleven thousand times -

213
00:20:47.847 --> 00:20:52.047
MILES: was that if we did it properly, nobody would ever have to come.

214
00:20:52.127 --> 00:20:53.727
LAUREN: And you did it properly.

215
00:20:53.807 --> 00:20:58.007
MILES: I did it properly for three hundred and sixty-four days a year.

216
00:20:59.240 --> 00:21:00.140
LAUREN: Yeah.

217
00:21:07.270 --> 00:21:09.137
LAUREN: I'm not angry that you lied.

218
00:21:10.515 --> 00:21:11.415
MILES: You are.

219
00:21:11.906 --> 00:21:14.106
LAUREN: I'm a little angry that you lied.

220
00:21:16.390 --> 00:21:18.323
LAUREN: You didn't protect me, Miles.

221
00:21:19.934 --> 00:21:24.667
LAUREN: You just made sure that when it came, I'd be the one who was surprised.

222
00:21:43.240 --> 00:21:44.140
MILES: It does that.

223
00:21:45.462 --> 00:21:46.362
LAUREN: Does what.

224
00:21:47.513 --> 00:21:48.779
MILES: When it's about to.

225
00:21:51.210 --> 00:21:52.110
MILES: Lauren.

226
00:21:53.403 --> 00:21:54.303
LAUREN: Don't.

227
00:21:55.597 --> 00:21:56.497
MILES: Lauren.

228
00:22:03.360 --> 00:22:08.560
MILES: I have been so scared for so long that I forgot it was a thing that could end.

229
00:22:10.128 --> 00:22:13.595
MILES: I thought if I could just hold it - for long enough-

230
00:22:40.330 --> 00:22:45.597
LAUREN: Okay. That's what you've been saying. That's what you've been saying all night.

231
00:22:46.971 --> 00:22:49.904
LAUREN: Stay put. Do nothing. That's good, isn't it-

232
00:23:00.270 --> 00:23:01.170
LAUREN: Miles?

233
00:23:01.250 --> 00:23:02.450
MILES: That's not advice.

234
00:23:02.536 --> 00:23:03.436
LAUREN: What?

235
00:23:03.516 --> 00:23:08.183
MILES: That's not somebody warning us. That's - Lauren, that's word for word.

236
00:23:09.210 --> 00:23:10.543
MILES: That's clause three.

237
00:23:16.270 --> 00:23:19.470
LAUREN: Somebody over there is reading us our own Terms.

238
00:23:21.544 --> 00:23:23.477
MILES: Somebody over there has them.

239
00:23:37.150 --> 00:23:38.050
LAUREN: Down to what.

240
00:23:50.270 --> 00:23:54.337
MILES: Back door, alley, left, and you're on Weir in ninety seconds.

241
00:23:54.607 --> 00:23:58.473
MILES: Front door, you're on Cedar, and Cedar only goes two ways.

242
00:23:59.240 --> 00:24:00.140
LAUREN: Car?

243
00:24:00.254 --> 00:24:01.254
MILES: Car's on Cedar.

244
00:24:01.521 --> 00:24:03.121
LAUREN: So the car's decorative.

245
00:24:03.549 --> 00:24:06.083
MILES: The car's a place somebody would wait.

246
00:24:14.270 --> 00:24:16.537
LAUREN: How long have those been up there?

247
00:24:16.861 --> 00:24:18.061
MILES: Since we moved in.

248
00:24:18.233 --> 00:24:19.133
LAUREN: Six years.

249
00:24:19.213 --> 00:24:20.113
MILES: Yes.

250
00:24:20.193 --> 00:24:21.660
LAUREN: You packed one for me.

251
00:24:21.740 --> 00:24:22.640
MILES: I packed two.

252
00:24:32.270 --> 00:24:34.337
LAUREN: We're not allowed to have this.

253
00:24:38.369 --> 00:24:39.269
MILES: I know.

254
00:24:45.150 --> 00:24:46.650
[phone buzzes]

255
00:24:58.270 --> 00:24:59.170
MILES: Okay.

256
00:25:00.185 --> 00:25:01.085
LAUREN: Okay?

257
00:25:02.101 --> 00:25:04.034
MILES: I'm putting it in the drawer.

258
00:25:15.150 --> 00:25:16.650
[the refrigerator stutters]

259
00:25:24.210 --> 00:25:26.543
LAUREN: Money, coats, the label. What else.

260
00:25:26.952 --> 00:25:30.218
MILES: Nothing else. That's the whole point of the bags.

261
00:25:47.300 --> 00:25:48.200
MILES: When.

262
00:25:48.513 --> 00:25:51.513
LAUREN: Tonight. That's the lamp. That's your jacket.

263
00:25:53.061 --> 00:25:54.661
MILES: We didn't sleep tonight.

264
00:25:55.487 --> 00:25:56.387
LAUREN: No.

265
00:26:01.150 --> 00:26:02.650
[smoke alarm chirps]

266
00:26:04.150 --> 00:26:05.650
[the same chirp, from the living room]

267
00:26:18.150 --> 00:26:19.650
[the chirp again - from the device]

268
00:26:25.240 --> 00:26:27.173
LAUREN: It won't do anything for you.

269
00:26:27.253 --> 00:26:28.153
MILES: What?

270
00:26:28.233 --> 00:26:33.500
LAUREN: You put your whole hand on it and it kept talking. I walk past it, it wakes up.

271
00:26:33.580 --> 00:26:34.480
MILES: Lauren.

272
00:26:36.500 --> 00:26:37.400
LAUREN: I know.

273
00:26:40.270 --> 00:26:45.537
MILES: That's four. Don't answer it. That's four, Lauren, that's the one you've never-

274
00:26:46.291 --> 00:26:48.424
LAUREN: And five's yours. So we're even.

275
00:26:53.270 --> 00:26:56.337
LAUREN: If you want us to do something, show me where.

276
00:27:17.240 --> 00:27:21.707
LAUREN: That's the sign. Miles, that's the sign from the - that's the sign.

277
00:27:25.210 --> 00:27:26.410
LAUREN: Miles. What is it?

278
00:27:32.150 --> 00:27:33.750
MILES: That's where we came in.

279
00:27:37.270 --> 00:27:38.170
LAUREN: What?

280
00:27:38.555 --> 00:27:43.022
MILES: Room eleven. Second floor, end of the walkway. That's the crossing.

281
00:27:46.330 --> 00:27:47.797
LAUREN: I don't remember that.

282
00:27:49.104 --> 00:27:50.004
MILES: No.

283
00:27:50.617 --> 00:27:53.017
LAUREN: Miles, I don't remember any of that.

284
00:27:55.157 --> 00:27:56.057
MILES: I know.

285
00:27:57.240 --> 00:28:00.507
MILES: And I have never once known what to do with that.

286
00:28:12.300 --> 00:28:14.033
LAUREN: It told us not to go back.

287
00:28:14.113 --> 00:28:15.013
MILES: Yes.

288
00:28:15.093 --> 00:28:17.360
LAUREN: And then it showed us where to go.

289
00:28:17.440 --> 00:28:18.340
MILES: Yes.

290
00:28:18.420 --> 00:28:20.087
LAUREN: So one of those is a lie.

291
00:28:20.167 --> 00:28:21.067
MILES: Yes.

292
00:28:21.147 --> 00:28:22.047
LAUREN: Which one?

293
00:28:22.127 --> 00:28:23.027
MILES: I don't know.

294
00:28:23.107 --> 00:28:24.007
[her voice] Lauren.

295
00:28:33.270 --> 00:28:39.270
[her voice] I'm going to say something, and it's going to be unkind, and I'm sorry, and I'd do it again.

296
00:28:42.180 --> 00:28:45.113
[her voice] Count backwards for me. I'll be here at one.

297
00:29:08.270 --> 00:29:09.603
LAUREN: My mother said that.

298
00:29:10.150 --> 00:29:11.050
MILES: Lauren-

299
00:29:11.278 --> 00:29:15.145
LAUREN: My mother said that to me. Every night. Nobody knows that.

300
00:29:17.270 --> 00:29:21.537
LAUREN: I have never said that out loud. Not once. Not here. Not to him.

301
00:29:26.240 --> 00:29:27.140
[her voice] I know.

302
00:29:28.894 --> 00:29:30.361
[her voice] She said it to me too.

303
00:29:34.150 --> 00:29:35.650
[all sound stops]

304
00:29:35.730 --> 00:29:37.130
[her voice] Didn't she, [ - - - ]

305
00:29:41.210 --> 00:29:43.010
MILES: What did you just call her.

306
00:29:55.210 --> 00:29:56.110
LAUREN: What am I?

307
00:29:57.757 --> 00:29:59.024
[her voice] You're the one who-

308
00:30:02.150 --> 00:30:03.650
[everything goes quiet]

309
00:30:53.150 --> 00:30:54.650
[the deadbolt turns by itself]

310
00:31:35.240 --> 00:31:36.140
MILES: Back door.

311
00:31:36.220 --> 00:31:37.120
LAUREN: No.

312
00:31:37.200 --> 00:31:40.533
MILES: Lauren, the alley's clear, you go left and you're-

313
00:31:40.918 --> 00:31:41.818
LAUREN: No.

314
00:31:41.898 --> 00:31:42.798
MILES: Please.

315
00:31:43.240 --> 00:31:47.640
LAUREN: I'm not doing the part where you decide for me twice in one night.

316
00:31:51.270 --> 00:31:52.870
MILES: That's not what this is.

317
00:31:52.950 --> 00:31:54.817
LAUREN: That's exactly what this is.

318
00:31:54.897 --> 00:31:59.830
LAUREN: You've done it for six years. It's the only thing you're actually good at.

319
00:32:00.240 --> 00:32:04.173
LAUREN: Miles. We're doing this one together or we're not doing it.

320
00:32:08.180 --> 00:32:09.080
MILES: Okay.

321
00:32:11.000 --> 00:32:11.900
LAUREN: Okay.

322
00:32:21.210 --> 00:32:25.210
MILES: There's something you need to know before that gets to zero.

323
00:32:26.337 --> 00:32:27.471
LAUREN: Then say it fast.

324
00:32:28.270 --> 00:32:29.470
MILES: Nobody comes over.

325
00:32:29.763 --> 00:32:30.663
LAUREN: What?

326
00:32:30.758 --> 00:32:35.558
MILES: It's not against the rules. It's - Lauren, it isn't a rule, it's a fact.

327
00:32:37.300 --> 00:32:39.900
MILES: People don't cross. Things don't cross.

328
00:32:40.516 --> 00:32:41.416
LAUREN: We crossed.

329
00:32:41.505 --> 00:32:45.705
MILES: We came out. That's different. That's falling. Anyone can fall.

330
00:32:47.270 --> 00:32:51.937
MILES: Coming the other way costs something. It costs more than a person has.

331
00:32:52.246 --> 00:32:53.146
LAUREN: Meaning what.

332
00:32:53.226 --> 00:32:55.626
MILES: Meaning nothing comes through whole.

333
00:32:56.300 --> 00:33:02.300
MILES: So whatever is out there - whatever it used to be - it paid everything it had to stand on our step.

334
00:33:02.546 --> 00:33:05.879
MILES: And it did that on purpose. And it did it tonight.

335
00:33:10.270 --> 00:33:14.737
LAUREN: Miles, I have to ask you something and I need you to not manage me.

336
00:33:17.445 --> 00:33:18.345
MILES: Okay.

337
00:33:19.210 --> 00:33:20.110
LAUREN: That message.

338
00:33:21.802 --> 00:33:23.135
LAUREN: Did it come from me?

339
00:33:37.150 --> 00:33:38.050
LAUREN: Okay.

340
00:33:57.120 --> 00:33:58.020
LAUREN: Who are you?

341
00:34:01.300 --> 00:34:04.100
[her voice] I'm the one who left when they told me to.

342
00:34:08.611 --> 00:34:09.511
[her voice] Don't.

343
00:34:18.150 --> 00:34:19.650
[silence]

344
00:34:25.150 --> 00:34:26.650
[knocking - three, then two]

345
00:34:40.210 --> 00:34:41.110
LAUREN: Miles.

346
00:34:43.500 --> 00:34:44.400
LAUREN: Miles, what.

347
00:34:47.180 --> 00:34:48.080
[muffled, through the door] It's me.

348
00:36:03.150 --> 00:36:05.350
[system voice] Retrieval is already in progress.

